---
title: Working on manifolds
summary: Rotations and poses as first-class quantities; how values, tangent vectors and retractions look from the user's side.
order: 5
---

Not every quantity lives in $\R^n$. A rotation lives on SO(3) and a rigid-body pose on SE(3).
Skoro treats both as first-class quantity types: `Q<B, SO3>` and `Q<B, SE3>`.

## What changes for the user

- **Values are stored, derivatives are tangent.** An `SO3` value is a flattened $3\times 3$ matrix
  (9 floats), but its gradient, Jacobian columns, and optimizer steps have 3 coordinates. `SE3` is
  12 stored, 6 tangent.
- **Steps are retractions.** An update is $x \leftarrow \retr(x, \delta)$ rather than
  $x + \delta$. `PointMap::retract_flat` applies each quantity's own retraction.
- **Residuals use the inverse retraction.** A Gaussian on a group measures $x \ominus \mu =
  \invretr(\mu, x)$ and whitens it.

## Operations

`skoro-so3` provides differentiable `exp` (Rodrigues' formula), `log`, compose, rotate/unrotate,
and invert. `skoro-se3` composes these with a translation. See
[Operations on quantities](../../concepts/quantity-operations/).

> [!NOTE] Accuracy of the Gaussian on a group
> The Gaussian's Fisher root is exact on flat spaces and correct to second order in the dispersion
> on groups. See [Fisher scoring, curved manifolds](../../concepts/fisher-scoring/#curved-manifolds).

